      "standardized_narrative": "At 31 December 2022 the syndicate's opening gross claims outstanding was $724.298m. Analysis of the gross claims development triangle (2018-2020 columns) shows a net adverse prior-year development of $29.6m (approx. 4.09% of opening gross reserves), driven primarily by upward development in the 2019 and 2020 underwriting years. The movement reflects large-loss and catastrophe-related development (including prior years' hurricanes, wildfires and pandemic-related exposures), inflationary pressures and specific IBNR allowances taken for the Russia/Ukraine conflict. The report also highlights pockets of favourable prior-year development in classes such as Property D&F, Marine Hull, Marine Energy, Non-Marine Liability and Political Risk, but on aggregate the gross triangle shows a net strengthening of reserves.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "Included within net calendar year claims incurred of $193,957,000 (2021: $196,366,000) is a release of $7,883,000 in claims reserves established for losses incurred at the prior year end (2021: release $7,832,000).",
        "The calendar year result also benefitted from favourable incurred claims development on prior accident years from a number of classes, including Property D&F, Marine Hull, Marine Energy, Non-Marine Liability and Political Risk.",
        "We have made specific incurred but not reported (\"IBNR\") allowances for classes where there is potential for losses arising as a result of the ongoing Russia/Ukraine conflict.",
        "The total net cost to Syndicate 1969 of these allowances for the 2022 calendar year is $4.8m.",
        "The total net cost to the syndicate of these events for the 2022 calendar year exceeded the catastrophe allowance for the calendar year by $3.8m.",
        "Inflation, in all its forms including social inflation, continues to be a key theme of discussion and has been specifically factored into our reserving this year."
      ],
